From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:27:52 -0400
Subject: feat: new tabs at the top of the list, as a setting, and twelve Space
 colours

Tabs R62, settings T30 (GitHub issue 22): with "Open new tabs at the top
of the list" on, a new tab that Chromium would put at the end of the
strip -- Cmd-T, + New Tab, a bookmark or an address in a new tab -- opens
under + New Tab instead: below the Space's pins, above its older tabs, and
above a folder that heads the list rather than in it. TabStripModel asks
SpaceModel::NewTabIndexAtTop through SetNewTabIndexCallback when a tab is
added with no place asked for; a link's tab keeps its place by its page.
Off by default (stedding.tabs.new_at_top), so the list is as it was.

Spaces B40: twelve Space colours in place of five, designers' colours
rather than ours: Radix Colors' solid steps (step 10 of the light scale
where step 9 is too pale on a light sidebar) and Tailwind's slate-500,
both MIT, none of them amber. The first five keep the old ones' hues and
order; a Space saved with one of the old five takes its new neighbour
when it is read back (UpdatedSpaceColor). The welcome flow's swatches
wrap to a second row.

Welcome W3, W4, W5, W13, W14, W15 (the owner, 2026-10-24: a better
first-run screen, and ask people to make Stedding the default browser):
the flow opens on a welcome screen ahead of step 1, with Get started and
Skip setup; the header names the six steps over short bars; the
appearance step's choices are drawings of a Stedding window in each look,
tinted by the Space colour chosen below them; the default-browser step
asks with one large button beside a drawing of a link opening in
Stedding; each step's title has a glyph; the importer rows carry marks as
the engines do; every control shows an amber ring with the keyboard
focus. Drawn by the page in boxes and SVG paths, in the brand's palette;
nothing is fetched.

Tests: PinnedRunTest.NewTabsOpenAtTheTopWhenAsked,
WelcomeFlowTest.TheFlowOpensOnAWelcomeScreen,
WelcomeFlowTest.TheDefaultStepAsksWithOneLargeButton.

Why: people coming from Arc keep their pinned tabs in view by opening new
tabs at the top (GitHub issue 22); the five muted Space colours were too
few and too alike (the owner, 2026-10-23).
Removable when: never; it is product behaviour.
